Vendored third-party dependency, moved to soroban-sdk 29
========================================================

  Library:  soroban-flux 0.1.0 (Rust, no_std)
  Upstream: https://github.com/nidohq/soroban-flux
  Release:  crates.io soroban-flux 0.1.0 (.crate sha256
            9273167cce4d4005c4eca46c3bb271ba4e681867b180bdc3f403ceb90170a731),
            published from commit 3170467df435aff14e9d7413659f4d04c25e5013
            ("feat: vendor the flux attribute stack — every crate now
            crates.io-publishable"), path crates/soroban-flux
  License:  Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE)
  Used by:  perch-program (Flux refinement attributes and extern specs)

Why vendored
------------
soroban-flux 0.1.0, its only release, requires soroban-sdk >=26.0.1, <28,
and no upstream branch moves it to 29 (checked 2026-11-03). Perch builds
with soroban-sdk 29.0.1 / soroban-env-host 29.0.1, and a crate that requires
another soroban-sdk major cannot share its types, so this copy is built as a
path dependency with the soroban-sdk pin moved. No change was proposed
upstream.

Upstream files
--------------
Every file is upstream's bytes except Cargo.toml (the published, normalized
manifest), whose delta is below. UPSTREAM.sha256 lists the sha256 of every
vendored file as published, with LICENSE taken from the repository root at
the commit above (the published crate carries none).

Not vendored: tests/, Cargo.lock, Cargo.toml.orig. The attribute crates it
depends on (soroban-flux-rs, soroban-flux-attrs, soroban-flux-attrs-impl
0.1.0) stay on crates.io: none of them links soroban-sdk.

SDK 29 delta
------------
Cargo.toml only:

  - `[dependencies.soroban-sdk]` version ">=26.0.1, <28" became "29.0.1";
  - the `[dev-dependencies]` table and the `[[test]]` target were dropped
    (the tests are not vendored).

The source compiles unchanged on soroban-sdk 29. CI's flux job (`cargo flux
-p perch-program`) checks perch-program against its extern specs.

Updating
--------
Replace the directory with the new upstream files, re-apply the delta above,
regenerate UPSTREAM.sha256 from the unmodified upstream files, and update
this NOTICE. crates/integration-tests/tests/vendor.rs requires every
vendored file other than Cargo.toml to hash to UPSTREAM.sha256 (after
reversing any source delta above) and the directory to hold nothing else but
NOTICE and UPSTREAM.sha256, so no other upstream byte can change unnoticed.
